   "title": "N. Korean leader's close aide visits Russia amid deepening bilateral ties",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/foreignaffairs/northkorea/20261115/n-korean-leaders-close-aide-visits-russia-amid-deepening-bilateral-ties",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:52:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794721923.0,
   "ageDays": 0.01,
   "summary": "A North Korean official considered to be one of North Korean leader Kim Jong-un's closest aides has arrived in Russia, the North's state media said Sunday, amid deepening relations between the two countries following North Korea's deployment of troops to support Russia's war against Ukraine. Jo Yong-won, secretary of the Central Committee of the ruling Workers' Party, arrived in Moscow by private plane on Saturday, leading a party and government delegation, the Korean Central News Agency said.",
   "summary_zh": "朝鲜国家媒体周日报道称，一名被视为朝鲜领导人 Kim Jong-un 最亲密助手之一的朝鲜官员已经抵达俄罗斯。此前，朝鲜派遣军队支持俄罗斯对乌克兰的战争，两国关系因此日益加深。朝鲜中央通信社称，执政的劳动党中央秘书赵容元（Jo Yong-won）于周六乘私人飞机抵达莫斯科，率领一个党政代表团。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "A North Korean official considered to be one of North Korean leader Kim Jong-un's closest aides has arrived in Russia, the North's state media said Sunday, amid deepening relations between the two countries following North Korea's deployment of troops to support Russia's war against Ukraine. Jo Yong-won, secretary of the Central Committee of the ruling Workers' Party, arrived in Moscow by private plane on Saturday, leading a party and government delegation, the Korean Central News Agency said. The visit comes at \"a time when the militant friendship, friendship and relations of alliance between the Democratic People's Republic of Korea and the Russian Federation with independence and justice as their common ideal are being further cemented with each passing day,\" it said in an English dispatch. The delegation was invited by Dmitry Medvedev, chairman of Russia's ruling United Russia party. They were greeted at the airport by Andrei Klimov, a member of the party's Supreme Council and first vice chairman of the International Affairs Committee of the State Duma, the lower house of Russia's parliament, as well as North Korean Ambassador to Moscow Sin Hong-chol. Speculation that Kim could visit Moscow this year surfaced when North Korea's foreign minister made a surprise visit to Russia in July. Jo's trip comes days before US President Donald Trump, Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin are set to meet on the sidelines of an Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit in Shenzhen, China, this week",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
