   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription The Delhi Police Special Cell has foiled a suspected firing plot targeting Bollywood actor Amitabh Bachchan outside his Mumbai residence, with the arrest of a shooter involved in the murder of Instagram influencer Mad Sandhu in Amritsar last month, officials said. Their arrests also helped avert a planned extortion-driven shooting targeting a Delhi-based businessman, the police said.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后即可解锁。德里警察特别行动小组挫获了一起针对宝莱坞演员阿米塔布·巴强住所的疑似枪击阴谋。官员表示，警方逮捕了一名枪手，该枪手涉嫌上月在阿姆利则杀害 Instagram 网红马德·桑德胡。警方称，此次逮捕还帮助挫败了一场针对一名驻德里商人的、以敲诈勒索为目的的预谋枪击案。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription The Delhi Police Special Cell has foiled a suspected firing plot targeting Bollywood actor Amitabh Bachchan outside his Mumbai residence, with the arrest of a shooter involved in the murder of Instagram influencer Mad Sandhu in Amritsar last month, officials said. The investigation into the arrests of two shooters linked to a foreign-based gangster has revealed that Deepak Singh alias Deep was instructed to remain in Mumbai for an extended period to execute the attack on the actor, allegedly over his purported remarks on the 1984 anti-Sikh riots, police sources said. Mr. Bachchan has consistently denied ever making any inciting remarks during the 1984 anti-Sikh riots. The two accused, identified as Vikas Thakur alias Vicky (25), a resident of Jalandhar, and Deepak Singh, a resident of Tarn Taran in Punjab, were arrested in separate intelligence-led operations in Delhi and Mumbai. Their arrests also helped avert a planned extortion-driven shooting targeting a Delhi-based businessman, the police said. According to the police, Vikas had travelled from Mumbai to Delhi on the instructions of the foreign-based gangster to carry out the shooting at the businessman. Deep was supposed to join him later. However, the Special Cell intercepted Vikas before the planned attack could be executed. Following his arrest, the police used intelligence inputs to track down Deep in Mumbai, where he was hiding after the October 3 murder of Mad Sandhu in Amritsar, Punjab. Deep is accused of carrying out the attack along with an associate, Palwinder alias Kaka, who has already been arrested by the Punjab Police. Deputy Commissioner of Police (Special Cell) Narra Chaitanya said the arrests had helped thwart two planned attacks and an extortion-related shooting. The police also said the timely intervention prevented an attack on the Bollywood actor. The police said Vikas had been working for different organised crime syndicates and had been tasked with arranging firearms, recruiting members and conducting reconnaissance of potential extortion targets. Born into a lower-income family, Vikas was academically sound during his early school years but allegedly fell into bad company in the absence of parental supervision. He first came to police notice as a juvenile in 2019 in a snatching case and subsequently became involved in illegal betting and gambling. In 2023, he began supplying illegal firearms to gangster Anmol Bishnoi. Following Bishnoi’s arrest, he shifted allegiance to gangsters Anil Pandit and Randeep Malik, undertaking various assignments, including arranging weapons, recruiting associates and conducting reconnaissance, the police said. He later began operating independently, taking up assignments from different gangs in return for money. He subsequently came in contact with the foreign-based gangster who tasked him with carrying out the firing on the Bollywood actor in Mumbai. Deep, meanwhile, had earlier worked as a commercial truck helper and driver. He was introduced to the foreign-based gangster through a local gang member and subsequently became involved in organised crime. The police said Deep and his associate Palwinder targeted Mad Sandhu in Amritsar on October 3 on the gangster’s instructions. While Palwinder was arrested by the Punjab Police, Deep fled and took shelter in Mumbai. The gangster subsequently instructed Deep to prolong his stay in Mumbai so that he could execute the planned firing on the actor. Vikas was also allegedly assigned the task of attacking the actor before being given the separate assignment targeting the Delhi businessman. A case under the Arms Act has been registered at the Special Cell police station (FIR No. 261/2026 dated November 3). Further investigation is under way. Hindi cinema / Mumbai / police / Maharashtra / arrest / crime, law and justice / shooting (crime) Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
